<title>USA: U.S. copper rod inventories down in April - ABMS.</title>
<headline>U.S. copper rod inventories down in April - ABMS.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Total copper inventories at U.S. rod mills (including cathodes, scrap, rod and in-process material) fell by the end of April to 120,281,000 lbs from a March tally of 122,982,000 lbs, the American Bureau of Metal Statistics said.</p>
<p>Rod production rose to 395,177,000 lbs from 354,881,000 lbs in March. Receipts totaled 400,611,000 lbs in April up from March's total of 392,619,000 lbs.</p>
<p>Total shipments rose to 407,413,000 lbs in April from 378,798,000 lbs the previous month.</p>
<p>	 ((--New York Commodity Desk 212-859-1640))</p>
